पुरोवर्तिनो निर्देशः Malli.); अमी रथ्याः Ś. 1. 8;\n अमी वह्नयः 4. 18, 7. 11. It is often used in the sense of\n तत् as a correlative of यत्; हिंसारतश्च यो नित्यं नेहासौ सुखमेधते\n "},{"t":"cite","s":"Ms. 4. 170","q":"Ms"},{"t":"txt","s":". He, who &c. But when it immediately follows the relative pronoun\n (योऽसौ, ये अमी &c.) it conveys the sense of प्रसिद्ध ‘well-known’,\n ‘celebrated’, ‘renowned’; योऽसावतीन्द्रियग्राह्यः सूक्ष्मोऽव्यक्तः सनातनः\n "},{"t":"cite","s":"Ms. 1. 7","q":"Ms"},{"t":"txt","s":"; योऽसौ कुमारसेवको नाम "},{"t":"cite","s":"Mu. 3","q":"Mu"},{"t":"txt","s":"; योऽसौ चोरः "},{"t":"cite","s":"Dk. 68","q":"Dk"},{"t":"txt","s":";\n sometimes अदस् used by itself conveys this sense; विधुरपि विधियोगाद्\n ग्रस्यते राहुणाऽसौ that (so well-known to us all) moon too. See the\n word तद् also and the quotations from K. P. ━ind. There, at that\n time, then, thus, ever; correlative to some pronominal forms; यदादः,\n यत्रादः whenever, whereever &c. By अदोऽनुपदेशे "},{"t":"sutra","s":"P. I. 4. 70","id":"1.4.70"},{"t":"txt","s":". अदस्\n has the force of a (गति) preposition when no direction to another\n is implied; अदःकृत्य अदःकृतम्; । परं प्रत्युपदेशे तु अदःकृत्वा अदःकुरु । Sk."}]}]}],"adasiya":[{"id":"adasIya","headword":"अदसीय","headword_slp1":"adasIya","senses_r":[{"n":1,"pos":"a.","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Belonging to this or that, Śāhendra. 2. 42."}]}]}],"adasyati":[{"id":"adasyati","headword":"अदस्यति","headword_slp1":"adasyati","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Den. P. To become that "},{"t":"sutra","s":"P. VIII. 2. 80","id":"8.2.80"},{"t":"txt","s":"."}]}]}],"adatf":[{"id":"adAtf","headword":"अदातृ","headword_slp1":"adAtf","senses_r":[{"n":1,"subs":[{"n":"1","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Not giving, miserly; आदाननित्याच्चादातुः "},{"t":"cite","s":"Ms. 11. 15","q":"Ms"},{"t":"txt","s":" not liberal"}]},{"n":"2","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Not giving (a daughter) in marriage; कालेऽदाता पिता वाच्यः "},{"t":"cite","s":"Ms. 9. 4","q":"Ms"},{"t":"txt","s":"."